# This is the "dot is disabled" feature

# One approach: before parsing, escape all "." to "\\."
# But then "\\." would match "\." which is wrong...

# The correct approach: use syntax.ClassNL flag which changes how "." is handled
# OR: post-process the Regexp to replace OpAnyChar/OpAnyCharNotNL with OpLiteral('.')

